      "detail": "swept lib/cpb for leaf-related substrings and found none. That is a substring sweep over .py files, not a proof of absence: it reads comments, and it would miss a leaf constructor written with binascii.unhexlify. The claim that this library constructs no leaf rests on its module set, canonicalize, derive_id, typed_ref, none of which does. Either way there is nothing there for this vector to accept or refuse, so it is scored on its own preconditions: 8/8 hold. Correct leaf_input 32 bytes, incorrect 64.",
