      "detail": "CPB verified the typed reference in every record that carries one (correct); the differing members are outside the cited artifact's digest context. ARP produced 5 distinct identifiers from 5 records. The CAID count is NOT reported beside it: caid.canonicalize is byte-identical to arp.jcs_bytes and the CAID digest field is 'sha256:' + the ARP subject digest, so it is the same digest in two encodings and not a second measurement. Diverging from base: registered_optional_field_memo, registered_optional_field_memo_empty_string, typed_digest_reference_added, optional_member_inside_the_typed_reference. 2 of those carry no typed reference at all, which is why the cause is ARP's whole-object digest and not CPB's ignore rule.",
